adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts the diff changes destinationCalendar to an array and introduces:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

When evt.destinationCalendar is null/undefined/[] the destructuring yields `mainHostDestinationCalendar === undefined`, so accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a TypeError. There is no `?.` guard on `mainHostDestinationCalendar` in this condition, so the crash is directly verifiable from the diff. The mention of handleNewBooking producing null is not necessary to establish the bug; even an empty array triggers it.

In `packages/core/EventManager.ts` within `createAllCalendarEvents`, the new per-destination loop has an `else` branch for destinations without `credentialId`:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(
  (c) => c.type === destination.integration
);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

After the diff, `createEvent` now accepts an optional third parameter `externalId?: string` and returns it as `result.externalId`, which is then used later as `externalCalendarId` in references (`externalCalendarId: result.externalId`). Because this branch calls `createEvent(c, event)` without passing `destination.externalId`, the created results will carry `externalId: undefined`, so subsequent references will have `externalCalendarId` undefined.

Also, because this `else` executes inside the `for (const destination of event.destinationCalendar)` loop, it will create events for *all* credentials matching `destination.integration` for each destination lacking `credentialId`. If there are multiple such destinations for the same integration, it will repeat creating events against the same set of credentials, producing duplicate events (an N×M-style multiplication).
